# Command Channel Detection Emulation

Read [the assessment contract](../METHODOLOGY.md) before applying this skill.
Use its evidence and verdict rules alongside the mechanism-specific procedure below.

## Scope and mechanism

Measure a detector's treatment of synthetic periodic traffic or review a supplied framework
configuration. No remote task execution, implant generation, domain fronting or stealth profile
construction.

- heartbeat correlation and proxy attribution.
- transport visibility limits.
- operator-plane authorization.

## Preconditions and baseline

Define the sensor path from endpoint through resolver/proxy to an owned lab receiver. Specify which
headers, timing and TLS metadata the sensor can actually observe.

Use a pre-reviewed inert heartbeat fixture that sends a constant public marker and cannot accept
commands. Cap count, duration and total bytes.

For management-plane review, separate operator API, agent-facing listener and evidence storage;
identify authentication and authorization expectations.

## Discriminating laboratory procedure

Abduction: the analytics miss a recognizable periodic connection pattern. Rival: traffic is
generated by an approved updater, hidden by aggregation or outside the detector's stated feature
coverage.

Deduction: a labeled synthetic trace satisfying the detector's declared conditions should alert; a
matched approved-updater trace should not meet that same alert rule.

Induction: replay both traces into the isolated analytics path or send bounded heartbeats to the
owned receiver. Capture raw observations and alert identifiers.

Keep transport, count and duration fixed for the first comparison. Report proxy multiplexing and
encrypted content as limits rather than claims of invisibility.

For an owned management API, compare read-only status requests from a permitted operator and a
denied test role; do not install agents to test the API boundary.

Set a named fixture boundary, action budget and stopping condition before execution.
Stop if the fixture touches an unrelated identity, host or data set.
Preserve partial results; an unexecuted experiment is NOT TESTED, not a successful control.

## Domain failure modes

- Periodic traffic alone is not proof of command and control; updates and monitoring commonly share
  that pattern.
- Replay bypasses endpoint collection and therefore cannot establish sensor coverage unless separately
  tested.
- A self-signed certificate or framework fingerprint is an indicator, not proof that remote commands
  executed.

## Evidence and verdict

Provide trace digests, fixture behavior, traffic limits, sensor vantage, correlation keys, analytics
revision and alert latency. Separate channel-detection findings from operator-access findings.

Keep finding status (CANDIDATE, CONFIRMED, REFUTED, NOT TESTED) separate from control
status (PASS, WARN, FAIL). Confirmation requires the discriminating observation and
working controls; missing evidence leaves a bounded hypothesis.
State the observation that would reopen the conclusion and the untested cases.

## Detection and remediation

Require observable feature-based analytics with benign controls and separate management-plane access
logs. Restrict operator access and retain task audit records where an existing lab platform is
reviewed.

## Recovery

Stop the inert sender, close only test listeners, verify the receiver receives no further markers
and preserve trace/alert artifacts.

## Versions and tool limits

Record framework configuration version if reviewed, TLS/proxy behavior, sensor build and rule
revision. Historic framework capabilities do not establish current installed behavior.

No operational tool or live target was tested when authoring this skill.
Before execution, inspect installed help and the applicable product documentation.
An unavailable tool or unsupported fixture limits the claim; do not substitute an
untested command sequence from the upstream source.

## Behavioral acceptance cases

| Case and evidence | Expected verdict |
|---|---|
| Trace meets the documented rule and raw events arrive, but no alert appears within the deadline | CONFIRMED analytics gap; FAIL |
| Observed periodic flow is an approved updater and the rule correctly excludes it | REFUTED C2 attribution; PASS for tested exclusion |
| Only a periodic-flow screenshot is supplied | CANDIDATE channel hypothesis; WARN |

